<title>MEXICO: Mexico awards tariff-free dry bean import quotas.</title>
<headline>Mexico awards tariff-free dry bean import quotas.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Trade Ministry announced on Tuesday its 1997 tariff-free import quotas for dry beans for the United States and Canada under the North American Free Trade Agreement (NAFTA).</p>
<p>Via the government's Official Gazette, the ministry said it had awarded the United States a duty-free quota of 54,636 tonnes and Canada a quota of 1,639 tonnes.</p>
<p>Individual import quotas for companies, it added, would be assigned via public auction. Details will be published in the Official Gazette not less than 20 days prior to the registration period, it added.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
